    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, clearly food insecurity is a national issue, but like all national issues, they resonate here at home. I want to commend first and foremost both food share for their tireless work to bring our community together and ensure our neighbors are fed. I wish I could be there on the celebration this year. But that may not be possible because of the work we have to do in D.C. And there I was proud to bring home 250,000 to Connecticut food share to start up the neighborhood grocery program at Frog Hollow. This set up a pay which you can market to make sure that residents of all incomes have access to healthy food. But food share, Bank of America deserve an enormous amount of credit for the effort they have put forward. Every Connecticut resident deserves access to affordable, nutritious food, and I will always advocate for that in Congress.",
