    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, no question about it. And to your point, you know, at the end of the school year, you know, we find that we've had a program to keep kids fed, which passed. But at the end of the school year, kids are still faced with the same issue of hunger. And so we are, you know, we're proud to co-sponsor the universal school meals program, which long term will make sure that children of all income status will make sure that they go to school and they're able to get fed and able to function. We also, there's also an early childhood nutrition improvement act that Representative Bonamichi has put forward and I'm a strong supporter of that as well. Head Start programs and homeless shelters, greater access to nutritious meals and snacks by streamlining paperwork and the reimbursement process that uh, plagues a lot of our providers.",
